; onehotr_row_out_of_range: a row outside the grid extent must raise.
;
; The only row of a 1x4 grid is row 0. `usize::try_from(row)` accepts any
; positive row, and `row * cols` then wraps: 2^62 * 4 is exactly 0 modulo
; a 64-bit usize, so an unchecked VM would write a clean-looking one-hot
; constraint onto row 0 and halt successfully under `release` while it
; panicked under `ci-test`. This vector pins IndexOutOfBounds on every
; profile.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; rows
PUSH 4           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 4611686018427387904   ; row == 2^62; row * cols wraps to 0
PUSH 1                     ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
